# Offline oracle note — dfpt-incommensurate-si

## Intent

Twin for incommensurate finite-q DFPT phonons on diamond Si (PW LSDA, NC-UPF).
Atomiverse path: `cpu::pw::DfptPhonon` with `q_frac = {0.3, 0.0, 0.0}` →
direct `internal::dfpt_q_force_constants` (not supercell).

## Preferred CP2K twin (when binary available)

- Structure: 2-atom FCC Si, a = 5.43 Å
- Method: Quickstep or CP2K phonon / VIBRATIONAL_ANALYSIS at non-Γ q, or
  export dynamical matrix at fractional q ≈ (0.3, 0, 0) of the same cell
- Functional: LDA / PADE-like; comparable NC or GTH setup
- Record: ω(q) [cm⁻¹] (6 branches), wall time, CP2K version

## This host (2026-07-25)

CP2K binary **not available**. Pins are literature-biased windows + measured
ATV spectrum under the regression twin (see
`regressions/response/dfpt-incommensurate-si/REFERENCE.md`).
`perf_exempt=true` until a fair CP2K DFPT wall is recorded.

## Cite

Baroni et al., Rev. Mod. Phys. 73, 515 (2001);
Giannozzi et al., Phys. Rev. B 43, 7231 (1991).
